Subject: Practiced Offense: give the AI a target for the double strike / lifelink part
Why: The AI checks a spell's sub-abilities before casting it. The second half (Pump with
  KWChoice$ Double Strike,Lifelink) reads to PumpAi as +0/+0 with no keyword, because nothing in
  forge-ai looks at KWChoice, so getPumpCreatures finds no creature that would benefit and the
  whole spell is refused (Azorius Momo, baseline: seen in 184 games, cast in 0).
  AILogic$ ContinuousBonus makes PumpAi pick the AI's own creature with the highest power, the
  right target for double strike. The counters half (target yourself) already passed.
Measured: `mtgsim gauntlet decks/standard/meta/azorius-momo.txt --vs <the other ten meta decks> -n 100
  --seed 1`, default AI, Forge 7db198d72e, on 13 Nov 2026. Arm without patches: 44.9% (95% CI
  42-48%, 449-551). Arm with 0003, 0004 and 0005 together (Momo's three patches; their separate
  shares were not measured): 54.3% (51-57%, 540-455 of 995 decided; the other 5 were engine
  errors that 0008 fixes; with 0008 the full 1,000 come to 542-458, 54.2%, 51-57%).
  Difference +9.4 points, 95% CI +5.0 to +13.7, p < 0.001. Mirror on the patched engine
  (`match azorius-momo azorius-momo -n 200 --seed 1`): 50.0% (43-57%).
  Practiced Offense cast in 579 of 629 games where it was seen (0 of 613 without), 1,408 casts
  counting flashback.

